22. City Council request to the Government of Ontario to reduce the financial burden on the City of Toronto related to provincial social assistance programs, which is estimated to be $125 million annually, by eliminating the Housing Services Act Rent Scales to equalize the shelter benefit components of Ontario Works (OW) and the Ontario Disability Support Program (ODSP) for rent-geared-to-income (RGI) households residing in City-administered community housing, with those residing in the private market housing.

